[00:09.52]Old Wives’ Tales are those ‘helpful’ things that your grandparents say that are probably not true.
[00:17.02]They are things like, ‘If you watch a lot of TV, you’ll get square eyes’, ‘If you eat carrots, you’ll see well in the dark’, or ‘If you eat cheese at night, you’ll have bad dreams’.
[00:32.98]But are they nonsense or is there sometimes a little bit of truth in them?
[00:38.88]We decided to investigate more.
[00:42.40]Let’s start with a famous one: ‘An apple a day keeps the doctor away’.
[00:48.70]My grandma said this all the time.
[00:51.84]Well, of course everyone knows that fruit is an important part of a healthy diet.
[00:57.70]But can one apple really make a difference?
[01:01.44]A medical study from 2013 says ‘yes’.
[01:06.10]It found that if people over 50 eat an apple a day, their chances of a heart attack are much smaller than people who don’t.
[01:16.14]What about ‘Gain a child, lose a tooth’?
[01:19.80]They say that when a woman has a child, a tooth will fall out.
[01:26.36]Researchers at the New York University College of Dentistry studied more than 2,600 women between the ages of 18 and 64 with one or more children.
[01:39.70]And guess what?
[01:41.66]They found they had more problems with their teeth than women with no children, although they couldn’t say exactly why.
[01:51.02]My great uncle was a big believer that ‘fish is brain food’.
[01:56.54]He ate it all the time and he was a clever man, too.
[02:01.28]It looks like he might be right.
[02:04.60]Fish have a lot of omega-3 and omega-6 fats in their oil.
[02:10.30]Some scientists from Oxford studied 120 primary school children, and they discovered that the children who ate omega-3 and omega-6 made big improvements in their schoolwork.
[02:25.06]If you eat fish oil, it will help to prevent heart problems, too.
[02:30.32]It seems like eating fish is a good idea.
[02:34.68]Finally, what about those carrots?
[02:37.38]Can they really help your night vision?
[02:41.14]I’ve eaten them all my life, but I still walk into things when I get up in the night.
[02:47.24]Unfortunately, I can’t find anything to prove if this is right or wrong.
[02:52.56]I’ll keep looking and I’ll let you know as soon as I find out.
